Subject: [PATCH] HIP: temporarily retain the pre-8fc0376 MMQ activation sum

The November 13 source-refresh screen isolates compact-graph nonthinking
replay sensitivity to the auxiliary activation sum introduced by upstream
8fc0376721e9662d498a5706d7ee8e7574ce99f4 (#31247). Same-binary selection of
the old sum bits restores the bounded replay without changing quantized
bytes, producer/consumer objects or samplers. This is numerical-trajectory
sensitivity, not evidence that the upstream correction is mathematically
wrong or that the former sum is generally more accurate.

Temporarily retain the pre-correction floating-input sum only in the HIP
quantize_mmq_q8_1 producer, for both normal and scatter instantiations.
Keep scale and quantized-byte generation unchanged. Non-HIP MMQ, the scalar
quantize_q8_1 producer, and the newer few-row MMQ producer retain upstream's
corrected behavior. There is no runtime switch or broadened fusion gate.

Removal gate: the corrected HIP sum must pass the unchanged compact-graph
nonthinking replay, ordinary/speculative and non-speculative gateway tests,
numerical/state checks, and the applicable long-context and hardware
acceptance matrix without relaxing numerical or output oracles. This narrow
compatibility mitigation does not establish broad model-quality equivalence.
See docs/hardware-acceptance.md for the held refresh and mechanism evidence.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu
index 2acf1f6..a87bf2f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu
@@ -500,6 +500,22 @@ static __global__ void quantize_mmq_q8_1(
         amax = fmaxf(amax, __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, amax, offset, WARP_SIZE));
     }
 
+#if defined(GGML_USE_HIP)
+    // Temporary HIP compatibility: the compact-graph replay is sensitive to
+    // this auxiliary sum. Keep the pre-8fc0376 MMQ value until the unchanged
+    // replay and broader acceptance pass with the upstream corrected sum.
+    float sum = 0.0f;
+    if (ds_layout != MMQ_Q8_1_DS_LAYOUT_D4) {
+        sum = xi.x + xi.y + xi.z + xi.w;
+
+        // Calculate sums across vals_per_sum/4 threads.
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int offset = vals_per_sum/8; offset > 0; offset >>= 1) {
+            sum += __shfl_xor_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, sum, offset, WARP_SIZE);
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     const float d_inv = 127.0f / amax;
     char4 q;
     q.x = roundf(xi.x*d_inv);
@@ -508,6 +524,7 @@ static __global__ void quantize_mmq_q8_1(
     q.w = roundf(xi.w*d_inv);
     const float d = 1.0f / d_inv;
 
+#if !defined(GGML_USE_HIP)
     float sum = 0.0f;
     if (ds_layout != MMQ_Q8_1_DS_LAYOUT_D4) {
         int sum_q = int(q.x) + int(q.y) + int(q.z) + int(q.w);
@@ -520,6 +537,7 @@ static __global__ void quantize_mmq_q8_1(
 
         sum = d * float(sum_q);
     }
+#endif
 
     // write the block once (normal) or to each of the token's compact rows (scatter)
     const int nwrite = scatter ? n_expert_used : 1;
